=begin pod

=NAME LLattice

=SUBTITLE Lawful lattice values and host-implementable Vinary Tree providers

=head1 SYNOPSIS

=begin code :lang<raku>
use LLattice;

my $low = MaxMin.new(value => 3);
my $high = MaxMin.new(value => 8);
say $low.join($high).value;
validate-laws([$low, $high]);
=end code

=head1 TYPES

=head2 Lattice

The exported role requires C<join> and C<meet>. Both accept another value from
the same lattice and return a new immutable value.

=head2 MaxMin

A numeric lattice in the ordinary total order. C<join> is maximum and C<meet>
is minimum.

=head2 BooleanLattice

The two-element lattice. C<join> is disjunction; C<meet> is conjunction.

=head2 FiniteSetLattice

The finite powerset lattice. C<join> is set union and C<meet> is set
intersection. It does C<Iterable>, reports C<elems>, and supports set-style
smart matching.

=head2 VectorContentLattice

An order-preserving finite-content lattice matching the native C<Vec> surface.
Join appends previously unseen right-hand values; meet retains common values in
left-hand order. The type does C<Iterable> and C<Positional>. Use the exported
C<equivalent> routine when comparing the content quotient independently of its
presentation order.

=head2 OptionalLattice

Lifts another lattice with an undefined bottom value. Join keeps a defined
operand; meet is defined only when both operands are defined.

=head1 ROUTINES

=head2 validate-laws

=begin code :lang<raku>
validate-laws(@finite-witnesses --> Bool)
=end code

Exhaustively checks associativity, commutativity, idempotence, and absorption
over a non-empty finite witness set. It dies with the first counterexample.

=head2 equivalent

Compares built-in lattice values according to their mathematical carrier. For
C<VectorContentLattice>, this deliberately ignores presentation order while
requiring exactly the same deduplicated content.

=head2 provider

=begin code :lang<raku>
provider(
    Lattice:D $value,
    Str:D :$domain-id!,
    :&encode!,
    :&decode,
    Bool:D :$parallel = False,
    --> LatticeValue:D
)
=end code

Creates an owned resource provider. The domain identifier must encode to
exactly 16 ASCII bytes. C<encode> returns canonical bytes; an optional decoder
allows operations with another provider of the same domain. Callbacks are
synchronous and confined to Rakudo-owned threads.

=head2 value

Returns the Raku value behind an open provider created by this distribution.
It rejects foreign providers.

=head1 OWNERSHIP

Call C<.close> on providers and every result returned by C<.join>, C<.meet>,
C<.join-many>, or C<.meet-many>. Destruction is a fallback only. Exceptions are
contained before native control returns and surface as typed interop failures;
C<.diagnostic> retrieves the provider message.

=end pod
